        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Qoder usage provider",
        "body": "## Summary\n- add a Qoder provider backed by the documented `big_model_credits` usage endpoint\n- support `qoder.com` and `qoder.com.cn` with Chrome cookie import, manual Cookie headers, and token-account overrides\n- handle documented and current response shapes, fractional/member/shared quotas, string or numeric reset dates, cancellation, stale-cache retries, and regional fallback\n- register Qoder settings, CLI rendering, menu/widget behavior, icon resources, documentation, and regression coverage\n\nCloses #1590.\n\n## Live proof\nAuthenticated Qoder China run on exact head `af6efc3a68456ef2270e97e1819b0d1ab08fef3d`:\n\n```console\n$ GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 swift run CodexBarCLI usage --provider qoder --source web --format json --pretty\nBuild of product 'CodexBarCLI' complete!\n[\n  {\n    \"provider\" : \"qoder\",\n    \"source\" : \"Chrome Default / qoder.com.cn\",\n    \"usage\" : {\n      \"identity\" : {\n        \"providerID\" : \"qoder\"\n      },\n      \"primary\" : {\n        \"resetDescription\" : \"0 / 300 credits\",\n        \"resetsAt\" : \"2026-07-09T10:36:42Z\",\n        \"usedPercent\" : 0\n      },\n      \"secondary\" : null,\n      \"tertiary\" : null,\n      \"updatedAt\" : \"2026-07-01T15:12:34Z\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n\n$ rg -n \"Cookie|Authorization|sid=|token|secret|password|Bearer|qoder-account-token|email|user(id|name)?\" /tmp/qoder-exact-head-proof.json\n# no matches\n```\n\nThe first authenticated exact-head attempt exposed a real China response variant where `nextResetAt` is a numeric timestamp rather than an ISO 8601 string. Commit `af6efc3` accepts both seconds/milliseconds and the existing string forms; the rerun above then completed successfully without exposing credentials or account identity.\n\n## Screenshots\nAuthenticated contributor run (pre-fix UI; exact head removes the second Credits section):\n\n<img width=\"1044\" height=\"1176\" alt=\"Qoder provider settings showing qoder.com.cn cookie source and 0 / 300 credits\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b56e63c1-d719-4b3c-9667-5c467dfc0c1b\" />\n\n<img width=\"622\" height=\"888\" alt=\"CodexBar menu showing Qoder tab with 100% left and 0 / 300 credits\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d2910929-72d4-4944-a083-ad05ba18afbb\" />\n\n## Validation\nExact head: `af6efc3a68456ef2270e97e1819b0d1ab08fef3d`\n\n- authenticated Qoder China CLI fetch — passed (`Chrome Default / qoder.com.cn`, `0 / 300 credits`)\n- sensitive-output scan — no matches\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter QoderUsageFetcherTests` — 9 tests passed\n- `swiftformat Sources/CodexBarCore/Providers/Qoder/QoderUsageFetcher.swift Tests/CodexBarTests/QoderUsageFetcherTests.swift` — passed\n- `git diff --check` — passed\n\nPrevious maintainer validation on parent `b78f420`:\n\n- `swift test --filter Qoder` — 19 tests passed\n- `make check` — passed\n- `make test` — all 44 shards passed; one shard used the suite's clean built-in retry\n- `swift build -c release --product CodexBarCLI` — passed\n- bundled autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings\n- all 17 review threads answered and resolved\n",
